I think the problem is reading from one buffer from multiple asynchronous contexts at the same time, while not reading request as a whole, but reading some parts of it.

https://github.com/helix-editor/helix/blob/b20a5c4c0ef16bb0298d072ac7ac8450796b5954/helix-lsp/src/transport.rs#L111

this function call allows other asynchronous contexts to read from buffer while reading current message has not been finished yet.

And that's exactly what happened in this case, when previous message hasn't been processed yet, a new message processing have started, and when it was looking for `Content-Length`, it found body from previous unprocessed yet message.

I see two solutions
1. ~~Make `reader` in `recv_server_message` synchronous, so that other threads will not be able to read until full processing haven't finished.~~ That's a bad idea, it'll block other stuff that are currently running.
2. Implement some lock system.
